WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.479
Satellite radar sees the ocean day and night,
through any cloud cover,

00:00:04.559 --> 00:00:07.150
capturing wind streaks, convective cells,

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:10.536
and other atmospheric signatures on the sea surface.

00:00:10.616 --> 00:00:16.073
But teaching machines to read these images is hard,
because expert labels are scarce.

00:00:16.153 --> 00:00:21.609
This work asks whether self-supervised learning on
three million unlabeled Sentinel-1

00:00:21.689 --> 00:00:24.930
radar images can overcome that labeling bottleneck,

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:27.210
and honestly reports what it found.
